---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Waves Cheat Sheet | Free Wave Properties, Optics, Sound"
  description="Complete waves cheat sheet with wave properties, optics, and sound. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Waves<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Wave properties, optics, and sound. From basic wave motion to electromagnetic waves.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Wave Properties</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Basic Equations</h3>
        <pre><code>v = fλ
T = 1/f
v = √(T/μ) (string)
v = √(B/ρ) (fluid)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Wave Types</h3>
        <pre><code>Transverse&#58; oscillation ⊥ propagation
Longitudinal&#58; oscillation ∥ propagation
Electromagnetic&#58; no medium required
Sound&#58; longitudinal, requires medium</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Optics</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Reflection & Refraction</h3>
        <pre><code>n₁ sin θ₁ = n₂ sin θ₂ (Snell's law)
θ_i = θ_r (reflection)
n = c/v (refractive index)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Lenses</h3>
        <pre><code>1/f = 1/v + 1/u (lens formula)
M = -v/u (magnification)
Power = 1/f (dioptres)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Sound</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Sound Waves</h3>
        <pre><code>v = fλ (speed of sound)
v = 343 m/s (air at 20°C)
I = P/A (intensity)
β = 10 log(I/I₀) (decibels)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Doppler Effect</h3>
        <pre><code>f' = f(v ± v_o)/(v ∓ v_s)
v_o&#58; observer moving
v_s&#58; source moving</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Electromagnetic Waves</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>EM Spectrum</h3>
        <pre><code>c = fλ = 3 × 10⁸ m/s
E = hf (photon energy)
E = hc/λ
λ = h/p (de Broglie)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
